  <section>
    <h2>Quick Answer</h2>
    <p>The <strong>16th China International Aviation &amp; Aerospace Exhibition (Airshow China)</strong> will be held in Zhuhai, Guangdong, from <strong>December 7–13, 2026</strong>.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Visitor dates">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Visitor type</th><th scope="col">Dates</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Professional days</th><td>December 8–10, 2026</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Public days</th><td>December 11–13, 2026</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Professional visitors must register in advance. Public visitors use tickets for the public days.</p>
    <p>If you are traveling from outside China, you also need to plan how you will enter Mainland China. Some eligible travelers may be able to attend using China's <strong>240-hour visa-free transit policy</strong>. Zhuhai is within the permitted Guangdong travel area, but there is an important catch:</p>
    <p><strong>Zhuhai Airport itself is not currently a designated 240-hour visa-free transit entry port.</strong></p>
    <p>Eligible travelers may instead enter Guangdong through a designated port such as the <strong>Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao Bridge Port</strong>, <strong>Hengqin Port</strong>, Guangzhou Baiyun Airport, Shenzhen Bao'an Airport, or another eligible Guangdong port that fits their itinerary.</p>
    <p class="cta"><a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/#checker">Check your itinerary with the Jadebound 240-hour transit checker →</a></p>
  </section>

