    <p>The 2026 airshow also includes additional exhibition areas for unmanned equipment and maritime equipment. Confirm which exhibition area your credential or ticket covers before planning transportation.</p>
    <p>The <a href="https://www.airshow.com.cn/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">current official Airshow China website</a> and visitor instructions give the December dates above. Older official materials still show different dates, so use the current visitor pages when planning your trip.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="professional-visitors">Professional Visitors: Registration, Dates and Prices</h2>
    <p>Airshow China separates professional visitors from public visitors. Professional visitor credentials are intended for adults <strong>18 or older</strong> working in aviation, aerospace or related industries.</p>
    <p>Professional visitor registration opened October 19 and closes <strong>December 4, 2026</strong>. There is <strong>no onsite professional registration</strong>, so complete the process before arriving in Zhuhai. Foreign visitors may use their <strong>passport</strong> as the identification document when registering.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap pass-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Professional pass prices and validity">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Professional pass</th><th scope="col">Price</th><th scope="col">Validity</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Single-entry pass</th><td>RMB 1,000</td><td>Dec. 9</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Single-entry pass</th><td>RMB 1,000</td><td>Dec. 10</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Multi-entry pass</th><td>RMB 2,000</td><td>Dec. 8–10</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>The single-entry passes permit one entry on the selected date. The multi-entry pass allows repeated entry during the professional days.</p>
    <p>Read the <a href="https://www.airshow.com.cn/Category_1432/Index.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official professional visitor Q&amp;A (Chinese)</a> and <a href="https://www.airshow.com.cn/Category_1429/Index_1.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">individual badge instructions (Chinese)</a> before registering.</p>
    <p><strong>Professional badges are not collected at the airshow venue.</strong> The current official instructions say badge shipping closes <strong>November 27</strong>, while offline badge collection is available <strong>November 28–December 4</strong> at the postal compound, 1054 Renmin West Road, Xiangzhou District, Zhuhai (珠海市香洲区人民西路1054号邮政大院).</p>
    <p>Overseas badge delivery is not confirmed in these instructions. International visitors should contact the professional visitor team to arrange delivery or pickup before traveling.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="public-visitors">Public Visitors</h2>
    <p>Public days are <strong>December 11–13, 2026</strong>. Public tickets are separate from professional visitor credentials and cannot be used interchangeably.</p>
    <p>Foreign visitors should bring the <strong>original passport used for ticketing</strong>, because the <a href="https://www.airshow.com.cn/Category_1322/Index.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official visitor Q&amp;A (Chinese)</a> says admission is checked against the valid identity document used to purchase the ticket.</p>
    <p><strong>Check the <a href="https://piao.airshow.com.cn/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official Airshow China ticketing page (Chinese)</a> for current public ticket prices and availability.</strong></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="transit">Can You Attend Airshow China Using 240-Hour Visa-Free Transit?</h2>
    <p>Possibly. China's current 240-hour visa-free transit policy covers travelers from <strong>57 countries, including the United States, Canada, the United Kingdom and Australia</strong>, and permits short business and tourism activities.</p>
    <p>The basic route requirement is:</p>
    <p><strong>Country or region A → Mainland China → different country or region B</strong></p>
    <p class="table-hint">On smaller screens, swipe the route table sideways.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap route-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Transit route examples">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Example route</th><th scope="col">Transit route requirement</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>U.S. → Guangzhou → Zhuhai → Hong Kong</td><td>Route can qualify</td></tr>
          <tr><td>U.S. → Shenzhen → Zhuhai → Macau</td><td>Route can qualify</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hong Kong → Zhuhai → Macau</td><td>Route can qualify</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hong Kong → Zhuhai → Hong Kong</td><td>Does not qualify</td></tr>
          <tr><td>U.S. → Mainland China → U.S.</td><td>Does not qualify</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>These examples only illustrate the route requirement. Your nationality, passport, entry port, onward booking and other requirements must also qualify.</p>
    <p>For complete eligibility requirements, current entry ports and stay rules, see our <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/">China 240-Hour Visa-Free Transit Guide</a>.</p>
    <p><a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/#checker">Check your actual itinerary with the Jadebound transit checker.</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="entry-warning">
    <h2 id="entry-ports">Important: Zhuhai Airport Is Not a 240-Hour Entry Port</h2>
    <p><strong>Do not assume you can fly directly into Zhuhai Airport and begin a 240-hour visa-free transit stay there.</strong></p>
    <p>Zhuhai Airport is immediately beside the Airshow China venue, but it is <strong>not currently listed among the designated entry ports for China's 240-hour visa-free transit policy</strong>.</p>
    <p>Two designated entry ports in the Zhuhai area are:</p>
    <ul><li><strong>Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao Bridge Port</strong></li><li><strong>Hengqin Port</strong></li></ul>
    <p>Other designated Guangdong entry points include Guangzhou Baiyun International Airport, Shenzhen Bao'an International Airport, Shekou passenger port, Guangzhou Pazhou Ferry Terminal, Zhongshan passenger port and West Kowloon Station.</p>
    <p>Once admitted under the 240-hour policy through a qualifying Guangdong entry port, travelers may travel within the permitted Guangdong area under the policy. See the <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/">Jadebound 240-hour guide for the current complete port list</a>.</p>
    <p class="cta"><a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/#checker">Check your exact entry route before booking →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="hong-kong-macau">Combining Airshow China With Hong Kong or Macau</h2>
    <p>Zhuhai sits directly next to Macau and is connected to Hong Kong by the <strong>Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao Bridge</strong>, making it convenient to combine Airshow China with either destination.</p>
    <p>For the 240-hour transit rule, Hong Kong and Macau count as separate regions from Mainland China.</p>
    <h3>Hong Kong → Zhuhai → Macau</h3>
    <p>This route can meet the transit-route requirement because you enter Mainland China from Hong Kong and leave Mainland China for Macau.</p>
    <h3>Hong Kong → Zhuhai → Hong Kong</h3>
    <p>This does <strong>not</strong> meet the route requirement because Hong Kong is both the region immediately before and immediately after Mainland China.</p>
    <h3>U.S. → Zhuhai-area eligible entry port → Hong Kong</h3>
    <p>This can potentially meet the route requirement if the actual Mainland China entry port is eligible and your other requirements qualify. Landing at Zhuhai Airport itself does not qualify as a 240-hour entry.</p>
    <p>The Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao Bridge Port and Hengqin Port were added as designated 240-hour entry ports in November 2025. <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/#checker">Check your planned route with the Jadebound checker</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="invitation-letters">Can Airshow China Provide a Visa Invitation Letter?</h2>
    <p>Yes, for exhibitors and trade visitors. The official site says trade visitors should first register online for their badge and may then contact the organizer for a visa invitation letter.</p>
    <p>The <a href="https://www.airshow.com.cn/Category_1239/Index.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official English Airshow China Visa Information page</a> lists <strong>Ms. Kelly Tu</strong> at <a href="mailto:asckelly@126.com">asckelly@126.com</a> as the contact.</p>
    <p>The organizer's <a href="https://www.airshow.com.cn/Category_1219/Index_1.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official general contact page</a> lists a different email for Ms. Kelly Tu: <a href="mailto:tukw@airshow.com.cn">tukw@airshow.com.cn</a>. Both addresses appear on official pages; we have not confirmed whether both are monitored for visa invitation requests. Start with the address on the Visa Information page, and use the general contact address as an alternative if needed.</p>
    <p>The invitation letter supports a visa application but does not itself grant permission to enter China or guarantee that a visa will be issued.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="venue">Where Is Airshow China Held?</h2>
    <p>The main venue is:</p>
    <p><strong>Zhuhai International Airshow Center</strong><br />555 Jinhai Middle Road<br />Jinwan District<br />Zhuhai, Guangdong, China</p>
    <p>Chinese venue name: <strong lang="zh">珠海国际航展中心</strong><br />Chinese address: <span lang="zh">广东省珠海市金湾区金海中路555号</span></p>
    <p>The exhibition center is immediately beside <strong>Zhuhai Airport</strong>. Check your entrance against the <a href="https://www.airshow.com.cn/UploadFiles/SingleNode/Airshow%20China%202026%20Site%20Plan.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official 2026 site plan (PDF)</a> before traveling.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="transport">Getting to Airshow China</h2>
    <h3>From Zhuhai Airport</h3>
    <p>Zhuhai International Airshow Center is located immediately beside Zhuhai Airport. However, Airshow China uses special traffic controls during the event, so follow the <a href="https://zhjt.airshow.com.cn/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official 2026 transportation guide (Chinese)</a> rather than assume normal taxi or private-car access.</p>
    <h3>From Hong Kong</h3>
    <p>The <a href="https://www.airshow.com.cn/Category_1237/Index.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official Airshow China Getting There page</a> lists two main ways to reach Zhuhai from Hong Kong: ferry and the Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao Bridge. The organizer says the ferry journey is approximately <strong>1 hour 15 minutes</strong>. Confirm current services before booking.</p>
    <p><strong>If you are relying on 240-hour visa-free transit, decide your Mainland China entry port before booking your Hong Kong-to-Zhuhai transfer.</strong> See the <a href="#hong-kong-macau">Hong Kong and Macau route examples</a> and <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/#checker">check your itinerary</a>.</p>
    <h3>From Macau</h3>
    <p>Macau is immediately adjacent to Zhuhai and can be a practical destination before or after the airshow. If using 240-hour transit, remember that the exact border crossing and direction of travel are part of your immigration itinerary. See our <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/">transit guide</a> or <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/#checker">checker</a> before booking.</p>
    <h3>By Rail</h3>
    <p><strong>Zhuhai Airport Railway Station Exit 3 is unconfirmed.</strong> We could not access the <a href="https://www.airshow.com.cn/UploadFiles/SingleNode/Airshow%20China%202026%20Site%20Plan.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official 2026 site-plan PDF</a> during our November 6 check because the website's access verification blocked it, so we could not verify the Exit 3 detail. This does not mean Exit 3 is closed or incorrect. Follow the current official transportation guide and station signs for the exit and route to your airshow entrance.</p>
    <p>The current transportation guide includes rail, local Airshow shuttle routes, intercity routes, taxi/ride-hailing guidance, private-car/parking information and airport passenger guidance. Use the <a href="https://zhjt.airshow.com.cn/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official 2026 transportation guide (Chinese)</a> for current station, entrance and transfer arrangements.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Do Not Assume You Can Drive Directly to the Venue</h2>
    <p>Airshow China uses significant traffic controls during the event. The official transportation plan includes special transportation services and parking/access guidance.</p>
    <p>Unless you have confirmed parking and access arrangements, use official public transportation or Airshow transportation services instead of renting a car specifically for the event.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="hotels">Where Should You Stay?</h2>
    <h3>Near Zhuhai Airport / Jinwan</h3>
    <p>Best for visitors whose main priority is attending multiple airshow days with the shortest practical trip to the venue.</p>
    <h3>Central Zhuhai</h3>
    <p>A better choice if you also want restaurants, city access or other activities, but the commute to the airshow will be longer.</p>
    <h3>Macau</h3>
    <p>Macau can work well as a stop before or after Airshow China. But it is usually not ideal as a daily commuting base for a traveler relying on 240-hour visa-free transit, because leaving Mainland China ends that particular entry.</p>
    <h3>Hong Kong</h3>
    <p>Treat Hong Kong as a stop before or after the Zhuhai stay rather than a daily airshow commuting base. Daily cross-border travel adds immigration and transportation complexity.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="admission">What Should International Visitors Bring?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your <strong>original passport</strong>.</li>
      <li>Your professional visitor badge or public ticket linked to that passport.</li>
      <li>Any Chinese visa or documents supporting your visa-free entry.</li>
      <li>Saved Airshow China registration/ticket confirmation.</li>
      <li>Onward travel confirmation if relying on 240-hour transit.</li>
      <li>Your hotel information.</li>
      <li>The Chinese name/address of the airshow venue.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The organizer says visitors should carry the <strong>original valid identity document used when purchasing or registering for admission</strong>, including passports for foreign visitors.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="checklist">Airshow China 2026 Travel Checklist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Confirm whether you are attending professional or public days.</li>
      <li>Register for a professional visitor badge before the December 4 deadline if applicable.</li>
      <li>Arrange professional badge delivery or pickup before arriving at the venue.</li>
      <li>Buy the correct public ticket if attending public days.</li>
      <li>Bring the original passport used for registration or ticketing.</li>
      <li>Confirm whether you need a Chinese visa or qualify for another entry policy.</li>
      <li>If using 240-hour transit, verify your nationality, route and exact Mainland China entry port.</li>
      <li>Remember that Zhuhai Airport itself is not currently a designated 240-hour entry port.</li>
      <li>Save your hotel and venue information in Chinese.</li>
      <li>Review the official transportation guide shortly before the show.</li>
      <li>Check the official flight-demonstration schedule shortly before your visit.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The organizer says flight and demonstration schedules can change because of weather and air-traffic controls and are generally published close to the event.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <details><summary>When is Airshow China 2026?</summary><p>Airshow China 2026 runs December 7–13 in Zhuhai. Professional visitor days are December 8–10. Public visitor days are December 11–13.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can foreigners attend Airshow China?</summary><p>Yes. Foreign professional visitors can register using their passport, and foreign public visitors should use the original passport connected to their ticket when entering.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I attend Airshow China using 240-hour visa-free transit?</summary><p>Potentially. Your nationality, itinerary, entry port, onward booking and other requirements must qualify. Read the <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/">Jadebound transit guide</a> or <a href="/china-240-hour-visa-free-transit/#checker">check your itinerary</a>.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is Zhuhai Airport an eligible 240-hour visa-free transit entry port?</summary><p>No. Zhuhai Airport is not currently listed among the designated 240-hour entry ports. Choose an eligible Guangdong entry port appropriate to your itinerary.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I travel Hong Kong → Zhuhai → Macau under the 240-hour policy?</summary><p>That route can satisfy the requirement that the country or region before Mainland China be different from the country or region afterward, provided your nationality, entry port and other conditions also qualify.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does Hong Kong → Zhuhai → Hong Kong qualify?</summary><p>No. Hong Kong would be both the region immediately before and immediately after Mainland China.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can Airshow China issue a visa invitation letter?</summary><p>The organizer says invitation letters are available for registered exhibitors and trade visitors. Trade visitors must register online for a badge before requesting a letter.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I register as a professional visitor at the venue?</summary><p>No. The official professional visitor Q&amp;A says there is no onsite professional registration. Applications close December 4.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where is the Airshow China venue?</summary><p>The main venue is Zhuhai International Airshow Center in Jinwan District, next to Zhuhai Airport.</p></details>
  </section>

